Package: manby
Title: Vector Tilesets Like 'tippecanoe', Several Times Faster
Version: 0.2.8
Authors@R: c(
    person("Birk", "Skyum", email = "birk.skyum@pm.me", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("Mapbox Inc.", role = "cph", comment = "tippecanoe, which manby ports"),
    person("Protomaps LLC", role = "cph", comment = "tippecanoe"),
    person("The authors of the Rust crates that manby builds in", role = c("ctb", "cph"),
      comment = "listed in inst/AUTHORS of the source package from CRAN"))
Description: Builds vector tilesets in 'PMTiles' and 'MBTiles' from sf data
    frames, 'DuckDB' tables, 'Arrow' tables and files, with the tiles that
    'tippecanoe' makes from the same features. 'manby', a 'Rust' port of
    'tippecanoe', is built into the package from CRAN and in 'webR', and
    elsewhere the package runs the 'manby' program, which it downloads from
    the package's release on first use.
License: BSD_2_clause + file LICENSE
URL: https://birkskyum.github.io/manby/, https://github.com/birkskyum/manby
BugReports: https://github.com/birkskyum/manby/issues
Depends:
    R (>= 4.0)
Imports:
    jsonlite,
    nanoarrow,
    processx,
    stats,
    tools,
    utils
Suggests:
    arrow,
    DBI,
    dbplyr,
    dplyr,
    duckdb,
    sf,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0),
    withr
SystemRequirements: Cargo (Rust's package manager), rustc >= 1.90, to
    build manby into the package
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Encoding: UTF-8
